IMPORT prelude

-- Retirement and Re-employment Act 1993 (Singapore) -- what I can do if I am retired unlawfully or denied re-employment,
-- by when, what the Minister may order for me, and what my employer (or I) can be fined.
--
-- SEAT: the employee nearing, at or past retirement age.
--
-- PROVISIONS COVERED: s 8(1), (3), (6), (8) (age dismissal before the specified age: representations to the Minister,
-- what may be directed, the bar on damages, recovery of an unpaid amount), s 8A(1)-(4) (re-employment disputes, notice
-- to the Commissioner, mediation requests, the time limits), s 8B(1)-(4), (6), (12), (14) (representations to be
-- re-employed, the time limit after conciliation, the bars between routes), s 8C(1), (2) (Employment Claims Tribunal
-- claims), and the penalties and composition that touch me: s 4(3), s 8(7), s 8B(13), s 9(2), s 9A(2), s 9B(1), s 9C,
-- s 10(1).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation ("version in force from 1/7/2022"), as deposited at
-- ../../registers/source-bundle/RRA1993.txt. The latest amendment annotated is Act 38 of 2021, with effect from 1 July 2022.
--
-- NOT ENCODED: how the Minister or the Tribunal fixes an amount (ss 8(4), 8B(10), 8C(3)); the Commissioner's inquiry and
-- report (ss 8(2), 8B(5)); conciliation itself (s 8A(5)); the Minister's leave to go to mediation after representations
-- (s 8B(7), (8), (9)), beyond the outcome named below; delegation (ss 8(9)-(11), 8B(15)-(17)); investigation powers
-- (s 9(1), s 9A(1), (3)); which offences are compoundable (s 10(3) regulations, not deposited); s 9B(2) (obstructing an
-- entry, inquiry or investigation), whose penalty is s 9C as for s 9A(2).
--
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Written with the writing-l4-rules skill, from the seat of the employee, with the design defaults
-- ruled on 2026-10-18. No pipeline, no coverage table, no independent test pass, no human gate. It is not for public
-- use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Retirement and Re-employment Act 1993 -- remedies and penalties, from the employee's seat`

GIVEN `a` IS A NUMBER, `b` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the lower of` MEANS IF `a` AT MOST `b` THEN `a` ELSE `b`

§§ `8(1), 8A(1)-(4) -- what my complaint is, and where it goes first`

-- s 8(1): an employee "below the specified age" who considers he or she "has been unlawfully dismissed on the ground of
-- age" may, "within one month of the dismissal, make representations in writing to the Minister to be reinstated".
-- s 8A(4): a "re-employment dispute" is over (a) denial of re-employment for not meeting the s 7(1) criteria; (b) denial
-- under s 7C(1) for want of a suitable vacancy; (c) "the reasonableness of the terms and conditions of any re-employment
-- offer"; (d) "the reasonableness of the amount of any employment assistance payment".
-- s 8A(1): for (a) or (b), "first notify the Commissioner in writing ... no later than one month after the last day of
-- the employee's employment", before representations to the Minister under s 8B.
-- s 8A(2): an employee who "attains the specified age on or after 1 January 2012" and considers he or she was "dismissed
-- without just cause or excuse ... on or after the date the employee attains the specified age" must likewise first
-- notify the Commissioner within one month after the last day of employment.
-- s 8A(3): for (c) or (d), a "mediation request" to the Commissioner under the Employment Claims Act 2016 "not later than 6
-- months after the last day of the employee's employment", before a claim; s 8C(1): then, if a "claim referral
-- certificate" is issued, a claim with an Employment Claims Tribunal.
-- Gloss: the Commissioner is the Commissioner for Labour (s 2(1)); the Employment Claims Tribunal sits under the State
-- Courts Act 1970.
DECLARE `My complaint` IS ONE OF
    `I was dismissed on the ground of age before my specified age`
    `I was denied re-employment as not meeting the eligibility criteria`
    `I was denied re-employment because no suitable vacancy was found`
    `I was dismissed without just cause or excuse on or after my specified age`
    `the terms of my re-employment offer are unreasonable`
    `the employment assistance payment offered to me is unreasonable`

DECLARE `First step` IS ONE OF
    `written representations to the Minister to be reinstated`
    `written notice to the Commissioner, then representations to the Minister to be re-employed`
    `a mediation request to the Commissioner, then a claim in the Employment Claims Tribunal`

GIVEN `my complaint` IS A `My complaint`
GIVETH A `First step`
DECIDE `Where do I take my complaint first` IS
    CONSIDER `my complaint`
    WHEN `I was dismissed on the ground of age before my specified age`
        THEN `written representations to the Minister to be reinstated`
    WHEN `the terms of my re-employment offer are unreasonable`
        THEN `a mediation request to the Commissioner, then a claim in the Employment Claims Tribunal`
    WHEN `the employment assistance payment offered to me is unreasonable`
        THEN `a mediation request to the Commissioner, then a claim in the Employment Claims Tribunal`
    OTHERWISE `written notice to the Commissioner, then representations to the Minister to be re-employed`

DECLARE `Clock start` IS ONE OF
    `the dismissal`
    `the last day of my employment`

GIVEN `my complaint` IS A `My complaint`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How many months do I have for the first step` IS
    CONSIDER `my complaint`
    WHEN `the terms of my re-employment offer are unreasonable` THEN 6
    WHEN `the employment assistance payment offered to me is unreasonable` THEN 6
    OTHERWISE 1

GIVEN `my complaint` IS A `My complaint`
GIVETH A `Clock start`
DECIDE `From when are those months counted` IS
    CONSIDER `my complaint`
    WHEN `I was dismissed on the ground of age before my specified age` THEN `the dismissal`
    OTHERWISE `the last day of my employment`

-- "Within one month", "no later than one month", "not later than 6 months": the limit itself is in time. Months are a
-- number here (the caller counts them); calendar months are not modelled.
GIVEN `my complaint` IS A `My complaint`
      `months since the clock started` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I in time for the first step` IF
    `months since the clock started` AT MOST `How many months do I have for the first step` `my complaint`

-- s 8B(2): representations to the Minister "must be made no later than one month after the conclusion of any
-- conciliation conducted pursuant to section 8A(5)". (s 8B(1) says "at any time after any conciliation"; s 8B(2) is the
-- limit and is followed.)
GIVEN `months since conciliation concluded` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I in time to make representations to the Minister after conciliation` IF
    `months since conciliation concluded` AT MOST 1

§§ `8(1), 8A(2), 8B(1) -- which remedy is open to me`

-- s 8(1) is open only to an employee "below the specified age" at the dismissal. Note: s 4(2) protects only up to the
-- prescribed minimum retirement age, but s 8(1) reaches up to the specified age, which may be a higher contractual age.
GIVEN `my age when dismissed` IS A NUMBER
      `my specified age` IS A NUMBER
      `I consider I was unlawfully dismissed on the ground of age` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the age-dismissal remedy in section 8 open to me` IF
        `I consider I was unlawfully dismissed on the ground of age`
    AND `my age when dismissed` LESS THAN `my specified age`

-- s 8A(2), s 8B(1): only "an employee who attains the specified age on or after 1 January 2012"; the date falls on
-- 1 January, so the year I attained my specified age decides it.
GIVEN `the year I attained my specified age` IS A NUMBER
      `I was dismissed on or after attaining my specified age` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I consider the dismissal was without just cause or excuse` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the just-cause remedy in section 8B open to me` IF
        `the year I attained my specified age` AT LEAST 2012
    AND `I was dismissed on or after attaining my specified age`
    AND `I consider the dismissal was without just cause or excuse`

§§ `8(3), 8B(6), 8B(7) -- what the Minister may direct for me`

-- s 8(3): if, after any Commissioner's report, "the Minister is satisfied that the employee has been unlawfully dismissed
-- ... on the ground of age", the Minister may direct the employer (a) "to reinstate the employee ... and to pay ... an
-- amount that is equivalent to the salary that the employee would have earned"; or (b) "to pay such amount of salary as
-- compensation as the Minister may consider just and equitable".
-- s 8B(6): if "the Minister is satisfied that the employee has been unreasonably denied of re-employment ... or dismissed
-- ... without just cause or excuse", the Minister may direct the employer (a) "to re-employ the employee"; or (b) "to pay
-- such amount of compensation as the Minister may consider just and equitable".
-- The judgment is the Minister's, so the answer is conditional on it; and both limbs are "may", so this names what may be
-- directed, never what will be.
DECLARE `Minister's route` IS ONE OF
    `representations under section 8`
    `representations under section 8B`

DECLARE `What the Minister may direct` IS ONE OF
    `reinstatement with the salary I would have earned, or just and equitable compensation`
    `re-employment, or just and equitable compensation`
    `no direction, unless the Minister is satisfied`

GIVEN `the route` IS A `Minister's route`
      `the Minister is satisfied, after any report of the Commissioner, that my complaint is made out` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `What the Minister may direct`
DECIDE `What may the Minister direct my employer to do for me` IS
    IF NOT `the Minister is satisfied, after any report of the Commissioner, that my complaint is made out`
    THEN `no direction, unless the Minister is satisfied`
    ELSE CONSIDER `the route`
         WHEN `representations under section 8`
             THEN `reinstatement with the salary I would have earned, or just and equitable compensation`
         WHEN `representations under section 8B`
             THEN `re-employment, or just and equitable compensation`

-- s 8(6), s 8B(12): a direction of the Minister "operates as a bar to any action for damages by the employee in any
-- court" in respect of the dismissal or denial. (s 8(5), s 8B(11): the Minister's decision "is final".)
GIVEN `the Minister has given my employer a direction` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I still sue my employer for damages over it` IF
    NOT `the Minister has given my employer a direction`

-- s 8(8), s 8B(14): where an amount directed "is not paid in accordance with the direction of the Minister and the
-- employer has been convicted" (under s 8(7) or s 8B(13)), the unpaid amount "is recoverable by the court as if it were a
-- fine and the amount so recovered is to be paid to the employee".
GIVEN `my employer has not paid what the Minister directed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `my employer has been convicted of failing to comply` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can the court recover the unpaid amount for me as if it were a fine` IF
        `my employer has not paid what the Minister directed`
    AND `my employer has been convicted of failing to comply`

§§ `8B(3), 8B(4), 8C(2) -- choosing one route closes the others`

-- For an employee "who is dismissed": s 8B(3) representations under s 8B(1) bar a Tribunal claim over the amount of the
-- employment assistance payment (s 8A(4)(d)) and representations under s 35(3) of the Industrial Relations Act 1960;
-- s 8B(4) representations under that s 35(3) bar the other two; s 8C(2) a Tribunal claim over the payment bars the other
-- two. Each "operate[s] as a bar ... in respect of that dismissal".
DECLARE `Route` IS ONE OF
    `representations to the Minister under section 8B`
    `representations under section 35(3) of the Industrial Relations Act 1960`
    `a Tribunal claim over the amount of the employment assistance payment`

GIVEN `the route` IS A `Route`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the route number` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the route`
    WHEN `representations to the Minister under section 8B` THEN 1
    WHEN `representations under section 35(3) of the Industrial Relations Act 1960` THEN 2
    WHEN `a Tribunal claim over the amount of the employment assistance payment` THEN 3

GIVEN `I was dismissed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the route I took first` IS A `Route`
      `the route I now want` IS A `Route`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the route I now want closed to me` IF
        `I was dismissed`
    AND NOT (`the route number` `the route I took first` EQUALS `the route number` `the route I now want`)

§§ `4(3), 8(7), 8B(13), 9(2), 9A(2), 9B(1), 9C, 10 -- penalties`

-- s 4(3): age dismissal below the prescribed minimum retirement age -- "a fine not exceeding $5,000 or ... imprisonment
-- for a term not exceeding 6 months or ... both". s 8(7), s 8B(13): failing to comply with the Minister's direction --
-- $10,000 or 12 months. s 9B(1): obstructing an employee "in appearing before the Commissioner pursuant to any summons" --
-- $5,000 or 6 months. Those are my employer's offences against me.
-- Two can be mine: s 9(2) hindering or obstructing an investigating officer or making to one a statement "false in any
-- material particular" -- $5,000 or 6 months; s 9A(2) neglecting to attend as a summons requires, which states no
-- penalty, so s 9C applies: $5,000 or 6 months, "and for a subsequent offence under the same section" $10,000 or
-- 12 months.
DECLARE `Offence` IS ONE OF
    `my employer dismissing me on the ground of age before my prescribed minimum retirement age`
    `my employer failing to comply with the Minister's direction under section 8`
    `my employer failing to comply with the Minister's direction under section 8B`
    `my employer obstructing me in appearing before the Commissioner under a summons`
    `my obstructing or making a false statement to an investigating officer`
    `my neglecting to attend as a summons requires`

GIVEN `the offence` IS A `Offence`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does the general penalty in section 9C apply` IF
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `my neglecting to attend as a summons requires` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `the offence` IS A `Offence`
      `it is a subsequent offence under the same section` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the maximum fine` IS
    IF `Does the general penalty in section 9C apply` `the offence`
    THEN IF `it is a subsequent offence under the same section` THEN 10000 ELSE 5000
    ELSE CONSIDER `the offence`
         WHEN `my employer failing to comply with the Minister's direction under section 8` THEN 10000
         WHEN `my employer failing to comply with the Minister's direction under section 8B` THEN 10000
         OTHERWISE 5000

-- In every penalty in this Act the $10,000 fine goes with 12 months and the $5,000 fine with 6 months.
GIVEN `the offence` IS A `Offence`
      `it is a subsequent offence under the same section` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the maximum imprisonment, in months` IS
    IF `What is the maximum fine` `the offence` `it is a subsequent offence under the same section` EQUALS 10000
    THEN 12
    ELSE 6

-- s 10(1): an investigating officer, with the Commissioner's approval, may compound an offence "prescribed as a
-- compoundable offence" for "a sum not exceeding the lower of" (a) "one half of the amount of the maximum fine that is
-- prescribed for the offence"; (b) "$1,000". Which offences are prescribed is in regulations not deposited, so this is
-- the most that could be collected (from me or my employer) IF the offence is compoundable.
GIVEN `the offence` IS A `Offence`
      `it is a subsequent offence under the same section` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the most a composition can cost, if the offence is compoundable` IS
    `the lower of`
        (`What is the maximum fine` `the offence` `it is a subsequent offence under the same section` DIVIDED BY 2)
        1000
